  ],
  "usage": "Give qty (good units), currency, pcbUnit and pcbNre, bom rows {part, per (qty per unit), price, moq, attr (attrition %)}, SMT placements and price per placement, hand work, assembly setup, enclosure unit and tooling, cable and test/packing per unit, freight for the order, yieldPct and amortize (spread one-time costs). Money values are plain numbers in the chosen currency. It returns the cost per unit, order total, units to build, NRE, the per-category breakdown, BOM lines with buy quantities and MOQ excess, and a table of other quantities. Use it for a first production quote or to see where the unit cost goes.",
  "sources": [
    "Ulrich & Eppinger, Product Design and Development, ch. 13 Design for Manufacturing (unit cost = components + assembly + overhead; amortized tooling)",
    "Rule of thumb: SMT attrition 1-5 % for small reeled parts; placement pricing per component from typical PCBA quotes"
  ]
}
